       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release).\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. That's a risk for severe GI effects and lactic acidosis.\n\nWas a different dose intended? Some possibilities:\n- **500 mg three times daily** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, split into doses such as 850 mg twice daily\n\nIf you confirm the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, I'll enter it with the note \"with meals.\""
